octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":557,"digest":"sha256:371948c04ebad71dfc41e3ba261ca15c6ed64e65026fcb5be1c09881f12d93fc","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-11-26T04:53:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-26T04:53:25Z"}],"body":"This release fixes MySQL and MariaDB filters and sorts on columns named like a function or a reserved word, and makes the MySQL monitor's row lock wait read safer.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- On MySQL and MariaDB, filters, filters by value, sorts and the column names completion\n  offers in the filter dialog always quote column names, so a column named like a function\n  (for example `current_role`) or a reserved word is read as the column. A condition typed\n  with such a function's name bare is kept as written.\n- The MySQL monitor reads row lock waits only when its connection confirms the server's version\n  and reaches the server directly. Behind a proxy that reports another version, or a pooler, the\n  Locks view says they are not read instead of risking a stalled server.\n- The MySQL monitor refuses a server version it cannot read instead of misreading a very large\n  one.\n\nThe archives are for macOS and Linux (arm64 and x86_64) and Windows (x86_64); SHA256SUMS lists their checksums. The Windows build is untested: CI builds it and runs its tests, but nobody has used datarig on Windows yet.\n\n\n## What's Changed\n* refactor(core, tui): the table tab's filter dialog, completion and error position ask the engine's rules by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/555\n* fix(core, tui): MySQL and MariaDB filters and sorts always quote the names they write by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/558\n* refactor(core, drivers, tui): a server's plan format is the engine's rules by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/566\n* refactor(core, drivers): monitor actions are the engine's rules by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/567\n* refactor(core, tui): the monitor's words are the engine's terms by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/568\n* fix(core, drivers): the MySQL monitor reads row lock waits only on a confirmed direct server by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/569\n* fix(core): the MySQL monitor refuses a version number it cannot hold by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/571\n* chore(release): 0.42.1 by @DokaDev in https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/pull/572\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DokaDev/datarig/compare/v0.42.0...v0.42.1","mentions_count":1}
